positions.description:
LocationESTEC, Noordwijk, Netherlands Description
Thermal Engineer in the Thermal Control Section, Thermal Division, Mechanical Department, Directorate of Technology, Engineering and Quality.

The Thermal Control Section provides functional support to ESA projects and carries out technological research (R&D) in the field of thermal control, two-phase heat transport and thermal protection.

The Section is part of a key centre of competence in space thermal engineering, covering the complete temperature range and staffed with around 25 engineers supporting all ESA projects and the development of thermal hardware technologies.

The Section offers a unique opportunity to contribute to solutions to the thermal challenges required for ESA missions, spacecraft, instruments and equipment, and is very active in knowledge management.Duties
Reporting to the Head of Section and within the technical fields described above, your main tasks and responsibilities will include:

providing expert technical support and consultancy to ESA projects, programmes and general studies in the field of thermal control throughout all project phases;
participating in feasibility studies, project reviews and the evaluation of procurement proposals;
performing analysis as required to support the thermal subsystem definition;
participating in thermal testing activities and correlating analysis and test results;
identifying critical development problems and assisting in their resolution;
contributing to the definition of technology development requirements and work plans for the Agency’s technology programmes;
defining, initiating and managing R&D activities covering both long- and short-term needs;
fostering new application areas for multidisciplinary activities, placing emphasis on innovative concepts, cutting-edge technologies and system architectures;
laboratory activities as required;
monitoring applicable scientific and technological trends and maintaining state-of-the-art expertise;
contributing to the dissemination of the results of the activities performed and the transfer of knowledge across the Agency.

Your duties may also include supporting other activities within your field of expertise.Technical competencies
General background and experience in the technical domains covered by the positionHands-on hardware experienceUnderstanding of related technologies, R&D trends and the industrial landscapeProject support experience in a relevant domainEnvironmental testing for space hardwareExperience in the preparation of procurement activities for technology development and innovation, such as statements of work and proposal evaluationBehavioural competencies
Result OrientationOperational EfficiencyFostering CooperationRelationship ManagementContinuous ImprovementForward Thinking
For more information, please refer to the ESA Core Behavioural Competencies guidebookEducation and professional experience
A master’s degree in mechanical engineering or physics is required for this post together with at least 4 years of relevant professional experience.Additional requirements
Experience in spacecraft thermal engineering, related technologies and a general knowledge of space thermal control analysis tools, such as ESATAN-TMS, is required.
 Diversity, Equity and Inclusiveness ESA is an equal opportunity employer, committed to achieving diversity within the workforce and creating an inclusive working environment. We therefore welcome applications from all qualified candidates irrespective of gender, sexual orientation, ethnicity, religious beliefs, age, disability or other characteristics. 
At the Agency we value diversity, and we welcome people with disabilities. Whenever possible, we seek to accommodate individuals with disabilities by providing the necessary support at the workplace. The Human Resources Department can also provide assistance during the recruitment process. If you would like to discuss this further, please contact us via email at contact.human.resources@esa.int. Important Information and DisclaimerIn principle, recruitment will be within the advertised grade band (A2-A4). However, if the selected candidate has less than four years of relevant professional experience following the completion of the master’s degree, the position may be filled at A1 level.
Applicants must be eligible to access information, technology, and hardware which is subject to European or US export control and sanctions regulations & eligible to acquire the security clearance by their national security administrations.
During the recruitment process, the Agency may request applicants to undergo selection tests. Additionally, successful candidates will need to undergo basic screening before appointment, which will be conducted by an external background screening service, in compliance with the European Space Agency's security procedures.
Note that ESA is in the process of transitioning to a Matrix setup, which could lead to organisational changes affecting this position.
The information published on ESA’s careers website regarding working conditions is correct at the time of publication. It is not intended to be exhaustive and may not address all questions you would have. 

Nationality and Languages Please note that applications are only considered from nationals of one of the following States: Austria, Belgium, Czechia, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Ireland, Italy, Luxembourg, the Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovenia, Spain, Sweden, Switzerland, the United Kingdom and Canada, Cyprus, Latvia, Lithuania and Slovakia. 
According to the ESA Convention, staff shall be recruited on the basis of their qualifications, taking into account an adequate distribution of posts among nationals of the Member States.
The working languages of the Agency are English and French. A good knowledge of one of these is required. Knowledge of another Member State language would be an asset.

positions.descriptionHtml:
Du willst nicht nur Betriebe führen, sondern eine Region verantworten, Teams entwickeln und aktiv zur Weiterentwicklung eines wachsenden Systems beitragen? Dann ist das deine Rolle.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Als Area Manager übernimmst du die unternehmerische Verantwortung für mehrere Standorte und stellst sicher, dass diese nicht nur stabil laufen, sondern sich kontinuierlich weiterentwickeln.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>Deine Rolle: Du bist verantwortlich für die Performance deiner Region – operativ, personell und strukturell. Du sorgst dafür, dass unsere Betriebe heute funktionieren und morgen besser sind.&nbsp;
<ul><li>Verantwortung für mehrere Standorte und Teams&nbsp;</li><li>Direkte Zusammenarbeit mit dem Head&nbsp;of&nbsp;F&amp;B&nbsp;</li><li>Hoher Gestaltungsspielraum in deinem Verantwortungsbereich&nbsp;</li><li>Möglichkeit, aktiv am Aufbau und an der Weiterentwicklung eines wachsenden Systems mitzuwirken</li><li>Ein wachsendes Unternehmen mit klarer Identitätund starkem Brand</li><li>30% Mitarbeiterrabatt &amp; regelmässige Team-Events</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Performance &amp; Ownership:</strong>&nbsp;Du führst mehrere Betriebe (ca. 4–6 Standorte) und&nbsp;trägst die Verantwortung für die&nbsp;wirtschaftliche Performance deiner Standorte.&nbsp;Du steuerst deine Region über KPIs, erkennst Abweichungen früh und leitest klare Massnahmen ab. Du stellst sicher, dass Umsatz, Kosten und operative Qualität im Gleichgewicht sind.</li><li><strong>Führung &amp;</strong><strong>Teame</strong><strong>ntwicklung:</strong>&nbsp;Du führst&nbsp;und entwickelst unsere&nbsp;Filialleitungen&nbsp;und baust starke, eigenverantwortliche Teams auf. Du&nbsp;sorgst für klare Strukturen und Verantwortlichkeiten in deinen Betrieben.&nbsp;Du identifizierst Talente und entwickelst diese gezielt weiter.</li><li><strong>Operative Exzellenz:</strong>&nbsp;Du stellst sicher, dass Qualität, Service und Abläufe in allen Standorten auf konstant hohem Niveau sind. Du bist regelmässig vor Ort, erkennst Probleme früh&nbsp;und greifst aktiv ein. Du sorgst dafür, dass Standards nicht nur definiert, sondern konsequent gelebt werden.</li><li><strong>Weiterentwicklung des Systems</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;Du bringst aktiv Feedback aus den&nbsp;Betrieben&nbsp;ein und trägst zur Weiterentwicklung von Prozessen und Konzepten bei.&nbsp;Du identifizierst Verbesserungspotenziale und setzt diese strukturiert um.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Zusammenarbeit &amp; Schnittstellen</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;Du arbeitest eng mit dem Head&nbsp;of&nbsp;F&amp;B sowie&nbsp;Marketing, Produkt und weiteren&nbsp;Bereichen zusammen und stellst sicher, dass Vorgaben und Initiativen in deinen&nbsp;Betrieben&nbsp;umgesetzt werden.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Mehrjährige Erfahrung in der Gastronomie, idealerweise in einem Multi-Unit-Umfeld&nbsp;</li><li>Erfahrung in der Führung von Teams oder mehreren Standorten&nbsp;</li><li>Stark im operativen Geschäft mit gutem Verständnis für Kennzahlen und Performance-Steuerung&nbsp;</li><li>Fähigkeit, Verantwortung zu übernehmen und selbstständig Entscheidungen zu treffen&nbsp;</li><li>Strukturierte, lösungsorientierte und konsequente Arbeitsweise</li><li>Hohe Präsenz, Durchsetzungsvermögen und Umsetzungsstärke&nbsp;</li><li>Sprachen: Deutsch fliessend, Englisch &amp; Französisch von Vorteil</li></ul>
<strong>Was uns wichtig ist&nbsp;</strong><ul><li>Du denkst in Verantwortung, nicht nur in Aufgaben&nbsp;</li><li>Du erkennst Probleme früh und gehst sie konsequent an&nbsp;</li><li>Du entwickelst deine Standorte und Teams aktiv weiter&nbsp;</li><li>Du übernimmst Ownership für Resultate – nicht nur für Umsetzung&nbsp;</li><li>Du bist nah am Betrieb und gleichzeitig klar in deinen Entscheidungen&nbsp;</li></ul>&nbsp;<br>Du möchtest mehrere Standorte aktiv führen, Teams entwickeln und im Alltag echten Unterschied machen?&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>Dann passt du perfekt zu&nbsp;Tenz. Bewirb dich jetzt – wir freuen uns darauf, dich kennenzulernen.&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br><strong>Rahmenbedingungen&nbsp;</strong><br>Arbeitsort: Region Deutschschweiz mit hoher Präsenz in den Betrieben. Ergänzend regelmässige Tätigkeit in der Zentrale. Der Einsatz ist je nach operativen Anforderungen und Projekten flexibel.&nbsp;<br>Pensum: 100%&nbsp;
<strong>Tenz Momo</strong><br>EST. 2142<br><br><p>Tenz ist ein junges Schweizer Food &amp; Drinks Unternehmen mit Tibetischen Wurzeln, das auf tibetische Teigtaschen, sogenannte «Momo», spezialisiert ist. In Tibet gelten die Teigtaschen nämlich als Festessen, das mit viel Liebe gemeinsam zubereitet und mit noch mehr Liebe gemeinsam gegessen wird. Diese Kultur wollen wir auch in der Schweiz zugänglicher machen. Authentisch, aber doch auf unsere ganz eigene Art. Denn unsere Momo und auch die Art, wie wir sie präsentieren, sollen ganz uns entsprechen: einem frischen Mix aus Tibet und der Schweiz.<br>Und das scheint zu schmecken. Gestartet als Ein-Mann-Spendenprojekt von Tenzin Tibatsang um tibetische Projekte zu unterstützen, sind wir mittlerweile zu einem Familienunternehmen mit über 200 Mitarbeitenden angewachsen.</p><br><p>Unsere zentrale Produktion, die «Momofaktur», befindet sich am Tenz Hauptsitz in Zürich. Aktuell betreiben wir 15 Restaurants &amp; Take-Aways in der Deutschschweiz. Mit viel Liebe und Leidenschaft sind wir ausserdem an über 200 Veranstaltungen jährlich im Einsatz sowie kooperieren mit Schweizer Partnern wie Migros, Coop oder Felfel.</p>

positions.descriptionMarkdown:
Votre futur collectif

- Communauté Sud Est
- Collectif de 100 personnes
- Une communauté multi expertises
- Au sein de la maison du célèbre compositeur Darius Milhaud qui a rouvert ses portes à l’été 2023, en plein cœur d’Aix en Provence. Ancien logis du bras d’or bâtie en 1670, cette bâtisse provençale réhabilitée en haut-lieu de la création et de l’innovation compose avec son passé de lieu de rencontre et de foyer d’exploration musicale. Entre ses murs chargés d’histoire, elle invite les arts et la culture mais également nos équipes locales à travailler de concert autour d’espaces de travail, de sociabilité et de détente.
- Fort de nos multiples expertises et de notre ADN technologique, nous avons pour ambition de devenir l’acteur numérique incontournable de la région Sud-Est.
Vos nouveaux challenges pour ce poste :

Onepoint accompagne ses clients de la stratégie à l’exécution sur des programmes de transformation numérique à fort impact. Dans une logique de croissance régionale, nous souhaitons accélérer notre développement commercial Sud‑Est, en renforçant notre capacité à : identifier les opportunités, nourrir notre pipeline, qualifier les besoins et valoriser nos expertises auprès de nos clients et prospects.

Pour accompagner cette dynamique, nous recrutons un alternant Commerce / Business Development F/H afin de contribuer au développement de la visibilité et des opportunités business.

Les attentes de la fonction sont les suivantes :

- Développer le pipeline commercial (prospection & qualification)
- Participer à l’identification et à la cartographie de comptes cibles (ETI/PME, grands comptes, acteurs publics etc.) ;
- Contribuer à la qualification des besoins en lien avec les équipes opérationnelles ;
- Participer à des actions de prospection et au suivi des leads ;
- Structurer et mettre à jour les informations dans les outils de pilotage (suivi, relances, priorisation).
- Contribuer à la construction d’offres & à la préparation des rendez-vous
- Aider à préparer les rendez-vous commerciaux ;
- Contribuer à la création de supports : présentations, argumentaires, one‑pagers, cas clients, propositions de valeur ;
- Participer à la mise en forme et à la structuration de réponses à sollicitations (emails, notes de cadrage, synthèses).
- Développer la visibilité commerciale (réseau, évènements, contenus)
- Contribuer à l’organisation / participation à des événements (réseaux locaux, afterworks, conférences, webinaires) ;
- Aider à animer la visibilité sur les réseaux (notamment LinkedIn) : idées de contenus, mise en avant d’expertises, relais d’actualités ;
- Participer à la production de contenus “business” : tendances marché, signaux de transformation, pain points clients.
- Utiliser l’IA comme levier d’efficacité
- Participer à la promotion de nos expertises autour de l’IA auprès des clients et prospects, en étant capable de :
- Valoriser nos cas d’usage et notre proposition de valeur,
- Vulgariser des sujets complexes pour les rendre accessibles,
- Contribuer à des échanges commerciaux intégrant des dimensions IA ;
- Accompagner les équipes dans la mise en avant de l’IA dans nos projets (pitch, supports, storytelling client) ;
- Tester de nouvelles approches pour améliorer l’efficacité commerciale (structuration de messages, segmentation clients, priorisation des actions).
Votre profil et les expertises que vous souhaitez développer :

- Vous êtes étudiant en dernière année d'école de commerce / université et recherchez une alternance pour la rentrée prochaine ;
- Vous avez un goût réel pour le commerce : prospection, relation client, négociation, compréhension des enjeux business ;
- Vous aimez structurer : suivi, organisation, priorisation, rigueur dans les relances et le pilotage ;
- Vous êtes à l’aise à l’oral, curieux, proactif ;
- Vous avez une sensibilité pour les sujets digitaux / tech / transformation ;
- Vous avez une appétence entrepreneuriale, en phase avec l’ADN intrapreneurial de Onepoint ;
- Vous maîtrisez le français et l’anglais.
Notre processus de recrutement

- 1er échange avec Camille (Camille Lanéry | LinkedIn) ou Pauline (Pauline MORGANTI | LinkedIn) : échange sur vos souhaits et motivations, et présentation de l'entreprise (durée : 45 min, Teams ou présentiel)
- 2ème échange avec un expert ou une experte technique : questions techniques et descriptif de nos projets (durée : 1 heure, Teams ou présentiel)
- 3e échange avec un ou une partner : projection sur votre rôle au sein de Onepoint (durée : 1 heure, Teams ou présentiel)

positions.description:
Role: AI Regulatory Product Counsel 
Location: Amsterdam 
Reporting to: Group Head of Privacy, Digital & AI Governance 

Who We Are
You've ordered from Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. 
We Are Prosus. A global technology company. We power the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce brands and help billions of people buy, sell and transact every day across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond. 
Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across food delivery, quick commerce, fintech, and experiences. We are building the world's largest agentic workforce - with 60k + active AI agents, our people don't just use AI; they build it and are at the forefront of innovation. Our investment team backs what's next from robotics, drones to synbio.
Guided by our five values Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship, culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation;, we build, we test, we learn, we iterate. 

The Problem You’ll Solve
To support Prosus goals and ambitions to lead AI innovation and improve everyday life for billions across the globe through cutting-edge technology, we are seeking an AI Regulatory Product Counsel to join the Prosus Group Privacy, Digital & AI Governance team, as part of the Legal function. 
In this role, you will have the opportunity to partner with the Prosus AI team and the cross-functional teams to provide strategic advice and support for launches and regulatory matters related to AI deployments, in particular agentic AI. As a trusted advisor to the AI teams, you will collaborate with our digital&regulatory team, the corporate legal team, policy and compliance at the intersection of advanced AI and emerging AI regulations. In doing so, you will use AI tools to augment your and your team’s work.
Prosus has adopted a Group Policy on Data Privacy Governance and a Responsible AI Policy 
(available at www.prosus.com/privacy) that constitute the foundations of the global AI and Privacy Governance global programmes. 
As part of the Prosus Legal function and the Digital & Regulatory Team, reporting to the Group Head of Privacy, Digital & AI Governance, you will have the opportunity to: 

Engage with and continuously support the Prosus AI Team; 

Provide expert advice on matters related to the implementation of AI tools, agents, infrastructure etc., including contractual terms. 

Support the Digital&Regulatory Team in terms of understanding the latest technological advancements in AI;

Operationalise the Prosus global Responsible AI Policy and establish viable AI governance mechanisms and engagement models;

Support Legal Innovation through the deployment of AI in Legal Operations, including through AI agents; 

Engage with the Prosus Cybersecurity team to implement AI security requirements and implement privacy and security by design 

Support the Digital & Regulatory Team in terms of group wide activities to foster knowledge sharing and collaboration amongst Prosus group companies;

Assist in AI governance projects and capabilities to adhere to the EU AI Act;

Support the Prosus Group in terms of implementation of the EU AI Act and global AI legislative developments (including outside of Europe); 

Assist in public policy outreach through submissions to consultations, events and publications; 

What You Bring 
You take ownership, tackle challenges head-on, and always see possibilities. Ambiguity doesn’t slow you down. It fuels you. You challenge the status quo, deliver real results, and balance bold vision with hands-on execution.
You are data-driven, innovative, and see failure as a learning curve, not a setback. At Prosus, experimentation fuels growth, and insights shape the future.
You are not afraid to venture into new domains, geographies and cultures. AI Technology does not scare you - on the contrary, you embrace it. 

You have excellent communication skills and a strong command of written and spoken English;

You have a good understanding of the latest status of AI technology and are comfortable using a range of AI tools; 

You will be a legal partner to the AI teams, with ability to build strong working relationships with internal and external stakeholders.

You have a proactive mindset, adept at problem solving and ready to challenge the status quo; 

You hold at least one Master’s-level Degree in a relevant field, specifically Law, Technology; 

You have a minimum of 4 years of experience in advising on technology product launches and/or deployments, including experience of working across legal, policy, regulatory, and compliance teams and you have a track record on advising on deployments of AI technology;

You have subject matter expertise in European regulatory frameworks relating to AI;

You have a structured mindset and are very organized;

You thrive in a fast-paced, diverse and multicultural environment. 

Why Prosus?

Global Impact: Play a crucial role in shaping the future of deployment of AI at global organisation scale. Be part of a dynamic ecosystem of tech-led companies across markets, from emerging disruptors to established platforms, all working to create positive change at scale.

Growth Opportunities: Expand your expertise through high-stakes challenges within our diverse portfolio. You'll gain access to a network of businesses, leaders, and learning opportunities that span continents and industries.

Innovative Culture: Join a forward-thinking team that values strategic insights and bold ideas. You’ll operate at the intersection of venture-building, innovation, and investment, where experimentation is encouraged and cross-company collaboration drives breakthroughs.

Creative Environment: Engage in work that encourages creativity and constant improvement. We challenge assumptions, explore new frontiers, and believe great ideas can come from anywhere in our ecosystem.

Collaborative Atmosphere: Benefit from autonomy and self-management in a supportive, outcome-driven workspace. You’ll work alongside sharp, motivated peers across our Legal function and portfolio, all united by a shared ambition to move the needle.

Competitive Compensation: Enjoy a salary package that reflects your skills and contributions.

Comprehensive Benefits: From health and wellness to learning, commuting, and everyday perks, we offer a well-rounded package designed to help you thrive at work and beyond.

Legal Exchange Programme: opportunity to apply for the Legal Exchange Programme with Prosus Group companies; 

Expert Team and IAPP membership: the opportunity to join a team of experts in the Digital & Regulatory domain, IAPP membership, certifications and engagements. 

